{
    "background_story": "McSteamy was a magnificent steam locomotive built in the late 19th century. For decades, he chugged along the scenic countryside, carrying passengers and freight with pride. As the years went by, however, McSteamy began to feel the effects of involution - a gradual decline in his performance and efficiency. His once-mighty steam engine began to sputter, and his wheels creaked with a familiar groan. Despite efforts to revamp and restore him, McSteamy eventually found himself relegated to a museum, a relic of a bygone era. As he sat idle, he couldn't help but feel a sense of nostalgia for the days when he was the epitome of power and progress. McSteamy's story serves as a reminder that even the mightiest machines can fall victim to the inevitable forces of involution.",
